1
00:00:00,126 --> 00:00:01,335
What kind of daughter are you?

2
00:00:01,419 --> 00:00:03,587
Before you ask me
what kind of daughter I am,

3
00:00:03,671 --> 00:00:05,965
why don't you ask her
what kind of mother she is?

4
00:00:06,465 --> 00:00:07,591
Why'd you come here?

5
00:00:07,883 --> 00:00:10,386
Nanny Cora, can we stay here?

6
00:00:10,469 --> 00:00:13,097
We now have a solution to our problems.

7
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:14,640
-Enough!
-That's enough!

8
00:00:14,724 --> 00:00:15,891
That's enough!

9
00:00:15,975 --> 00:00:17,810
I just thought you've changed.

10
00:00:17,893 --> 00:00:19,103
But I thought wrong.

11
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:22,648
You don't need another
fake smiling campaign.

12
00:00:22,898 --> 00:00:24,233
What you need…

13
00:00:24,316 --> 00:00:26,277
is a tell-all sit-down interview.

14
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,404
The mother and daughter
will face each other.

15
00:00:28,487 --> 00:00:30,489
This Sunday on…

16
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:32,032
Uncovered.

17
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:35,536
Diana, Patricia, welcome to Uncovered.

18
00:00:35,619 --> 00:00:37,079
Welcome to the program.

19
00:00:37,163 --> 00:00:39,039
And thank you very much.

20
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:41,000
First, let's talk about…

21
00:00:41,083 --> 00:00:42,960
the video.

22
00:00:43,419 --> 00:00:44,879
What is this about?

23
00:00:46,505 --> 00:00:47,506
Oh, uh…

24
00:00:47,590 --> 00:00:50,426
It was just a big misunderstanding.

25
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:54,930
As you all know,
I was still recovering from an illness.

26
00:00:55,014 --> 00:00:56,182
And…

27
00:00:56,515 --> 00:01:00,853
I was quite disoriented
when I saw them at my house.

28
00:01:01,687 --> 00:01:04,106
But we've talked it all out.

29
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:05,566
I've made amends already.

30
00:01:05,649 --> 00:01:07,318
How did you…

31
00:01:07,401 --> 00:01:08,527
make amends?

32
00:01:10,112 --> 00:01:13,199
Okay, we'll talk about that later,
but before that,

33
00:01:13,282 --> 00:01:17,286
how does it feel that
you guys are reunited now?

34
00:01:18,412 --> 00:01:20,498
Well, we haven't been together
for a long time,

35
00:01:20,581 --> 00:01:22,833
so we're still adjusting.

36
00:01:23,918 --> 00:01:26,962
What matters is that my mother is safe.

37
00:01:27,713 --> 00:01:29,173
La Familia.

38
00:01:29,715 --> 00:01:32,176
But now that I'm talking to you…

39
00:01:32,885 --> 00:01:36,722
where is this family as we're speaking?

40
00:01:36,806 --> 00:01:40,100
As you know, my father was the one
who started La Familia,

41
00:01:40,184 --> 00:01:42,186
and I continued to run it.

42
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:43,854
And, uh…

43
00:01:44,313 --> 00:01:48,359
for me, it's not just a company.

44
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:50,820
Uh…

45
00:01:51,195 --> 00:01:52,321
It's about family.

46
00:01:52,404 --> 00:01:55,115
We may have some disagreements,

47
00:01:55,199 --> 00:01:57,827
but it's about the people
you care the most about.

48
00:01:57,910 --> 00:02:02,122
It's about the bonds that
survive time and distance.

49
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:05,835
Thank you.

50
00:02:05,918 --> 00:02:09,171
Patricia, you seem like
a devoted daughter.

51
00:02:10,005 --> 00:02:11,006
Um…

52
00:02:11,090 --> 00:02:13,676
Did you find it hard
to forgive each other?

53
00:02:14,885 --> 00:02:18,055
Well, you know,
forgiveness is not like a switch, right?

54
00:02:18,305 --> 00:02:21,392
You can't just turn it on or off.

55
00:02:21,475 --> 00:02:24,103
It's a decision, and…

56
00:02:25,104 --> 00:02:26,647
I choose my daughter.

57
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:31,402
And I chose to understand her as well.

58
00:02:32,945 --> 00:02:35,698
If she didn't have a heart attack…

59
00:02:36,490 --> 00:02:38,200
what do you think would be
your situation right now?

60
00:02:39,285 --> 00:02:41,161
We'd still be fighting.

61
00:02:41,245 --> 00:02:42,705
Just kidding.

62
00:02:42,788 --> 00:02:44,206
And still…

63
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:46,917
And still missing each other.

64
00:02:48,002 --> 00:02:49,712
Well, um…

65
00:02:49,795 --> 00:02:52,006
Diana, you won't be missing
Patricia anymore

66
00:02:52,089 --> 00:02:54,633
because I have it from good sources,

67
00:02:54,717 --> 00:02:58,262
that Patricia will be
working at La Familia.

68
00:03:15,821 --> 00:03:17,031
Yes!

69
00:03:17,489 --> 00:03:18,490
Are you excited?

70
00:03:19,658 --> 00:03:21,243
Very excited.

71
00:03:21,785 --> 00:03:23,245
It looks like…

72
00:03:23,787 --> 00:03:28,834
your daughter, Patricia,
will continue La Familia's legacy.

73
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:30,794
How do you feel about it?

74
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,132
That's what I've always wanted.

75
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:36,592
It's official.

76
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:38,719
Here at Uncovered,

77
00:03:38,802 --> 00:03:43,182
we are officially welcoming
Patricia to La Familia.

78
00:03:43,515 --> 00:03:46,393
Patricia, welcome back home.

79
00:03:57,488 --> 00:03:58,864
Okay, cut!

80
00:05:01,802 --> 00:05:03,012
What was that?

81
00:05:03,512 --> 00:05:06,557
Working at La Familia
wasn't part of the deal.

82
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:10,436
I thought we'd only do
a photoshoot and an interview.

83
00:05:10,894 --> 00:05:12,980
I'm just sticking with the narrative.

84
00:05:13,397 --> 00:05:17,735
Diana also said how important
legacy is to La Familia.

85
00:05:17,985 --> 00:05:19,737
Lip service is not enough.

86
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:21,780
Words without actions are meaningless.

87
00:05:22,406 --> 00:05:24,825
The people won't believe you.

88
00:05:26,702 --> 00:05:28,579
I have a job, okay?

89
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:30,622
What job?

90
00:05:30,706 --> 00:05:33,000
Your job is unstable.

91
00:05:33,876 --> 00:05:36,462
Patricia, you should play the part.

92
00:05:38,005 --> 00:05:39,923
Think of it as your biggest break.

93
00:05:40,007 --> 00:05:41,842
You will be paid as well.

94
00:05:42,217 --> 00:05:43,969
Don't you see it?

95
00:05:45,012 --> 00:05:48,015
There's a reason why
I stayed away from my mother.

96
00:05:52,019 --> 00:05:53,604
I'm not going to force you.

97
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:57,691
Do you have any other jobs
or opportunities to choose from?

98
00:05:58,817 --> 00:06:00,527
The million you will earn here

99
00:06:00,611 --> 00:06:03,906
is just enough to pay off
your father's debts.

100
00:06:04,198 --> 00:06:05,908
Will you earn that
while working as a talent?

101
00:06:05,991 --> 00:06:08,702
Fine, let's just say that you
continue working as a talent.

102
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:12,372
But we all know that
it is not a stable job.

103
00:06:12,456 --> 00:06:14,041
You won't always book a job.

104
00:06:14,291 --> 00:06:15,667
So, just think of…

105
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:18,295
what you will do in La Familia
as your training,

106
00:06:18,378 --> 00:06:20,881
as your fallback for your family.

107
00:06:21,298 --> 00:06:22,674
I am guiding both of you…

108
00:06:23,717 --> 00:06:26,595
towards a situation
that will benefit both of you.

109
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:28,931
It's not just Diana
who'll benefit from this.

110
00:06:29,014 --> 00:06:31,391
It will also change your life.

111
00:06:32,893 --> 00:06:35,354
What you're saying is additional work.

112
00:06:35,687 --> 00:06:37,272
That should incur additional payment…

113
00:06:37,689 --> 00:06:39,566
separate from the prior million.

114
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:42,402
I think that's workable.

115
00:06:52,579 --> 00:06:54,248
Was that part of your deal?

116
00:06:54,581 --> 00:06:56,083
You don't have to do that.

117
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:57,709
They said it's necessary.

118
00:06:58,710 --> 00:06:59,920
They will pay me.

119
00:07:00,003 --> 00:07:01,088
No.

120
00:07:01,505 --> 00:07:03,757
Just give them back the money.

121
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:08,345
The money that we need?

122
00:07:10,222 --> 00:07:11,306
Pa…

123
00:07:12,182 --> 00:07:14,393
Sir Ricardo is right.

124
00:07:15,185 --> 00:07:18,063
The money I make as a talent
is no longer enough.

125
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:20,440
They will pay me a lot of money.

126
00:07:20,524 --> 00:07:21,608
It will be help us a lot.

127
00:07:21,692 --> 00:07:24,653
We'll have money
for rent, electricity, water,

128
00:07:24,945 --> 00:07:26,905
April and Jena's tuition,

129
00:07:27,156 --> 00:07:28,407
for your medicines,

130
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:31,201
and all our other expenses here at home.

131
00:07:34,121 --> 00:07:35,497
Patricia…

132
00:07:35,789 --> 00:07:37,291
Are you sure?

133
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:42,004
Because, I'll warn you, I know Diana well.

134
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:44,798
She is very wicked. Can you handle it?

135
00:07:46,925 --> 00:07:49,678
We still have to see each other anyway.

136
00:07:49,761 --> 00:07:51,013
Why?

137
00:07:51,305 --> 00:07:53,098
To receive her payment.

138
00:07:56,727 --> 00:07:58,312
She said she'd pay me in installments.

139
00:07:59,897 --> 00:08:01,148
See?

140
00:08:01,231 --> 00:08:05,527
You know, Diana is just
on another level, isn't she?

141
00:08:06,028 --> 00:08:09,406
But, you know, you'll manage because…

142
00:08:10,282 --> 00:08:12,409
I raised you.

143
00:08:19,291 --> 00:08:21,710
We need to control the narrative.

144
00:08:22,211 --> 00:08:25,631
I want the interview
and the campaign everywhere.

145
00:08:25,714 --> 00:08:27,424
-Bro.
-Hm?

146
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:29,718
-Chairmom is your employer, right?
-Mm-hmm.

147
00:08:29,801 --> 00:08:31,845
Doesn't she look like
she really loves her daughter?

148
00:08:31,929 --> 00:08:33,764
What parent doesn't love their child?

149
00:08:34,223 --> 00:08:35,015
You have a point.

150
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:37,392
Pay top influencers…

151
00:08:37,893 --> 00:08:39,228
lifestyle vloggers,

152
00:08:39,311 --> 00:08:41,188
and mommy creators for reactions.

153
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:44,691
But the paid partnerships
should look organic.

154
00:08:45,192 --> 00:08:46,068
Hey, look.

155
00:08:46,193 --> 00:08:48,028
Patricia is just like my daughter.

156
00:08:48,403 --> 00:08:50,572
-She has a point, doesn't she?
-Yes.

157
00:08:50,656 --> 00:08:52,741
Boost positive engagement

158
00:08:52,824 --> 00:08:54,618
and drown out the negative noise.

159
00:08:54,910 --> 00:08:56,912
They argue just like us, don't they?

160
00:08:58,121 --> 00:09:00,832
I think I'm craving Cala Soda.

161
00:09:00,916 --> 00:09:02,000
-Should we buy some?
-Sure.

162
00:09:02,084 --> 00:09:03,335
All right.

163
00:09:04,419 --> 00:09:07,172
Anything defamatory or malicious,
flag it immediately.

164
00:09:07,506 --> 00:09:10,384
We won't allow hate to be trending.

165
00:09:12,386 --> 00:09:14,680
Patricia, I'll use your outfit, okay?

166
00:09:14,763 --> 00:09:16,598
-You can have it.
-Okay!

167
00:09:16,682 --> 00:09:18,600
Wait a minute.
Let's take a selfie, bestie.

168
00:09:18,684 --> 00:09:21,186
I'll make a vlog.
I have a famous friend now!

169
00:09:21,270 --> 00:09:22,729
Why are you taking photos
with just you two?

170
00:09:22,813 --> 00:09:23,939
Include us!

171
00:09:24,022 --> 00:09:25,983
Right! Go there.

172
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:32,614
We are officially welcoming Patricia…

173
00:09:33,198 --> 00:09:34,408
to La Familia.

174
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:37,244
Patricia, welcome back home.

175
00:09:58,307 --> 00:10:00,100
Since the launch of the campaign…

176
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,602
we've received a lot of positive comments.

177
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:05,981
The negative comments
are greatly outnumbered.

178
00:10:06,398 --> 00:10:08,692
Cala Soda is back at number one.

179
00:10:09,484 --> 00:10:10,485
So…

180
00:10:11,778 --> 00:10:12,946
Congratulations.

181
00:10:14,114 --> 00:10:15,866
I kept my promise.

182
00:10:18,243 --> 00:10:19,328
But I have to admit,

183
00:10:19,703 --> 00:10:21,705
this wouldn't have happened

184
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:23,498
if you and Patricia hadn't agreed to it.

185
00:10:24,166 --> 00:10:26,585
Your idea to take her into…

186
00:10:27,085 --> 00:10:28,545
La Familia…

187
00:10:29,087 --> 00:10:30,922
was a master stroke.

188
00:10:31,715 --> 00:10:33,508
That's why you're the Chairmom.

189
00:10:33,884 --> 00:10:36,428
Stop it with the empty flattery.

190
00:10:38,388 --> 00:10:41,433
Patricia shouldn't know
what we talked about.

191
00:10:43,518 --> 00:10:46,605
About her working at La Familia?

192
00:10:47,689 --> 00:10:49,733
Why did you decide to do that?

193
00:10:50,901 --> 00:10:53,153
Have you seen Patricia's life?

194
00:10:53,779 --> 00:10:55,614
She's still an Aragon.

195
00:10:56,198 --> 00:10:58,200
I won't let her life go astray.

196
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:00,577
I have to keep an eye on her.

197
00:11:00,827 --> 00:11:02,245
Just like a mother.

198
00:11:04,998 --> 00:11:07,334
Your one percent company share.

199
00:11:08,627 --> 00:11:12,005
You are La Familia's
new head of public relations.

200
00:11:13,006 --> 00:11:14,925
I've already signed the contract.

201
00:11:15,008 --> 00:11:16,927
Just return that to me
once you're done with it.

202
00:11:21,014 --> 00:11:24,184
But the issue about
the poisoning isn't over yet.

203
00:11:25,185 --> 00:11:27,562
We can't be distracted.
It all started there.

204
00:11:28,188 --> 00:11:30,148
There are still people
who don't accept the settlement.

205
00:11:30,899 --> 00:11:32,192
I want this to finally end.

206
00:11:32,609 --> 00:11:34,611
I looked into what happened.

207
00:11:34,986 --> 00:11:37,114
There were markers
for an organized demolition.

208
00:11:37,781 --> 00:11:39,908
We checked the other accounts.

209
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:43,328
This was all done within
the last week of the attack.

210
00:11:43,412 --> 00:11:45,414
The timing, the messages…

211
00:11:45,497 --> 00:11:46,706
someone controlled it.

212
00:11:47,124 --> 00:11:50,627
Are you saying that
the poisoning was planned?

213
00:11:50,919 --> 00:11:52,087
The question is…

214
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:54,256
who has a grudge against you?

215
00:11:54,673 --> 00:11:56,800
I think the better question is…

216
00:11:57,092 --> 00:11:59,136
who doesn't hold a grudge against me?

217
00:12:14,693 --> 00:12:16,111
Go ahead with the plan.

218
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,407
That's the first installment
for our payment.

219
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:22,993
Oh, finally.

220
00:12:23,618 --> 00:12:25,287
-Thank you.
-My goodness!

221
00:12:25,787 --> 00:12:28,206
Are you really going
to pay us in installments?

222
00:12:28,290 --> 00:12:29,875
We saw you on TV!

223
00:12:29,958 --> 00:12:31,501
You were even bragging to us

224
00:12:31,585 --> 00:12:33,503
that you were the child of a CEO!

225
00:12:33,587 --> 00:12:34,546
Right?

226
00:12:34,796 --> 00:12:36,715
Just be grateful that you're getting paid

227
00:12:36,798 --> 00:12:38,592
even if it's in installments.

228
00:12:38,675 --> 00:12:41,094
Wait a minute, when is your next payment?

229
00:12:41,595 --> 00:12:43,722
-Next month.
-Okay, fine.

230
00:12:43,805 --> 00:12:45,223
Just make sure to pay us!

231
00:12:45,307 --> 00:12:47,142
You might hide from us again.

232
00:12:47,225 --> 00:12:48,435
-Right!
-He's right!

233
00:12:48,518 --> 00:12:50,103
That will never happen.

234
00:12:50,187 --> 00:12:52,898
-Okay, fine. Let's get going.
-Thank you.

235
00:12:52,981 --> 00:12:54,566
-Pay us again next time.
-We'll be back.

236
00:12:54,816 --> 00:12:56,902
They finally paid.

237
00:13:04,910 --> 00:13:06,369
Have you decided yet, dear?

238
00:13:06,453 --> 00:13:07,496
Yes.

239
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:09,956
I will work at La Familia.

240
00:13:10,665 --> 00:13:11,791
We need the money.

241
00:13:12,209 --> 00:13:14,127
They told me that I could also keep doing

242
00:13:14,211 --> 00:13:15,504
what I'm already doing.

243
00:13:17,339 --> 00:13:20,717
Just make sure that they will
hold their end of the deal.

244
00:13:23,595 --> 00:13:25,305
It might be a good thing, too.

245
00:13:25,388 --> 00:13:26,348
How so?

246
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:31,228
Well, if Patricia would inherit
all of it anyway,

247
00:13:31,311 --> 00:13:33,730
then it would be better
if she would start training

248
00:13:33,813 --> 00:13:35,899
on how to run their business, right?

249
00:13:51,289 --> 00:13:52,874
Hey, cuz!

250
00:13:52,958 --> 00:13:55,043
So, the rumors are true.

251
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:56,586
You're going to work here.

252
00:13:58,797 --> 00:14:00,507
That's a good look on you.

253
00:14:01,007 --> 00:14:02,425
Very vintage.

254
00:14:02,509 --> 00:14:04,219
Very abstract.

255
00:14:04,511 --> 00:14:05,720
Very…

256
00:14:06,012 --> 00:14:07,556
grandmother's attic.

257
00:14:08,014 --> 00:14:09,099
It suits you.

258
00:14:09,182 --> 00:14:11,059
Hey, Georgia, we have to go.

259
00:14:11,518 --> 00:14:14,437
-Excuse me.
-We'll get going then.

260
00:14:14,521 --> 00:14:15,897
Bye!

261
00:14:22,904 --> 00:14:24,614
I love my life. I love my life.

262
00:14:24,698 --> 00:14:26,408
I love my life.

263
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:33,081
-Good morning, Ms. D.
-Ms. D?

264
00:14:33,707 --> 00:14:36,126
That's what your employees
call you, right?

265
00:14:36,209 --> 00:14:38,211
I'm now an employee of La Familia too.

266
00:14:38,295 --> 00:14:39,421
I don't want people to think that

267
00:14:39,504 --> 00:14:40,880
you're giving me any special treatment.

268
00:14:41,298 --> 00:14:43,008
I know where my station is.

269
00:14:44,009 --> 00:14:45,885
-Enzo.
-Yes, Ms. D?

270
00:14:46,386 --> 00:14:49,014
Brief Patricia on what her job entails,

271
00:14:49,097 --> 00:14:51,975
and especially the dress code.

272
00:14:52,309 --> 00:14:53,727
-Copy, Ms. D.
-We're right on time!

273
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:55,520
Ms. D and Patricia are already here.

274
00:14:55,604 --> 00:14:56,521
Ah, sorry. Excuse me.

275
00:14:56,605 --> 00:14:57,731
Patricia!

276
00:15:00,108 --> 00:15:01,818
Welcome to La Familia.

277
00:15:03,111 --> 00:15:06,406
The only daughter's
first day at La Familia.

278
00:15:06,489 --> 00:15:09,117
Picture, picture! Take your photos.

279
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,118
Let's go, let's go.

280
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:11,911
Smile, smile.

281
00:15:12,579 --> 00:15:13,913
Keep taking photos, guys.

282
00:15:18,710 --> 00:15:19,711
You there!

283
00:15:20,795 --> 00:15:23,048
Hurry up!

284
00:15:24,299 --> 00:15:27,552
-What's going on?
-Diana Aragon! Come out!

285
00:15:27,636 --> 00:15:28,928
-Come and face us!
-What?

286
00:15:29,012 --> 00:15:30,388
-What's happening? What's going on?
-Give us justice!

287
00:15:30,472 --> 00:15:32,140
I'll call security, Ms. D.

288
00:15:32,807 --> 00:15:34,142
Security!

289
00:15:35,810 --> 00:15:36,936
Patricia!

290
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:38,313
Where are you going?

291
00:15:38,563 --> 00:15:39,898
I'm going to talk with them.

292
00:15:40,190 --> 00:15:41,608
Are you out of your mind?

293
00:15:41,691 --> 00:15:43,818
Diana, let's go inside.

294
00:15:43,902 --> 00:15:45,236
There's a lot of press here.

295
00:15:45,612 --> 00:15:46,863
Let's go, let's go.

296
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:53,578
Let's go inside!

297
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,414
Didn't I assign this to you?

298
00:15:56,498 --> 00:15:58,416
But you prioritized the press earlier

299
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:01,211
to make a spectacle
out of me and my daughter.

300
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:03,421
I had a schedule to talk to them today.

301
00:16:03,505 --> 00:16:06,007
Maybe they've heard that
we had the press here,

302
00:16:06,091 --> 00:16:07,967
so they rushed to make some noise.

303
00:16:08,218 --> 00:16:11,721
Why didn't you just let me talk to them?

304
00:16:11,805 --> 00:16:14,974
Whatever you say could become a liability.

305
00:16:15,308 --> 00:16:18,019
That's why I don't just let
anybody talk with them.

306
00:16:18,311 --> 00:16:19,604
You need training for that.

307
00:16:19,688 --> 00:16:21,898
Besides, it's not part
of your job description.

308
00:16:22,524 --> 00:16:25,110
Then what am I really supposed to do here?

309
00:16:26,611 --> 00:16:27,946
Just follow Enzo's lead.

310
00:16:28,613 --> 00:16:29,781
And please,

311
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:31,866
can we do our jobs right this time?

312
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:42,877
Let me help you.

313
00:16:42,961 --> 00:16:44,212
No thanks, I can handle it.

314
00:16:44,504 --> 00:16:45,714
-Just give it to me.
-But…

315
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:53,513
I was just being kind earlier,
but I got reprimanded.

316
00:16:54,806 --> 00:16:57,058
This is the company's uniform room.

317
00:16:57,392 --> 00:16:59,519
We have a standard here
for business formal

318
00:17:00,019 --> 00:17:02,981
because Ms. D doesn't want
her employees to look sloppy.

319
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:04,566
Number one,

320
00:17:05,108 --> 00:17:07,068
neutral colors only.

321
00:17:08,194 --> 00:17:09,654
No loud colors, please.

322
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:12,240
It should also be well-fit.

323
00:17:13,408 --> 00:17:15,201
It's to avoid distractions

324
00:17:15,285 --> 00:17:18,788
because we all need
to only focus on our work.

325
00:17:19,205 --> 00:17:21,458
It's also your way of showing respect.

326
00:17:21,708 --> 00:17:23,209
Your respect for others.

327
00:17:23,293 --> 00:17:25,795
Your respect for the company you work for.

328
00:17:25,879 --> 00:17:28,089
And the respect you want
others to give you.

329
00:17:28,798 --> 00:17:31,050
So that's why you all look the same here.

330
00:17:33,511 --> 00:17:35,388
I'll give the employee manual
to you later.

331
00:17:35,972 --> 00:17:38,308
Read and understand it carefully.

332
00:17:38,391 --> 00:17:39,517
It's important.

333
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:43,104
Wait a second.
I just want to clarify our deal.

334
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:46,399
I won't come in here
every day on a regular basis.

335
00:17:46,483 --> 00:17:49,402
I'm not going to stay here permanently.

336
00:17:50,487 --> 00:17:51,738
I have a life of my own.

337
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:54,199
But when you agreed to the deal,

338
00:17:54,407 --> 00:17:56,159
you also agreed to follow the rules.

339
00:18:05,794 --> 00:18:06,920
This suits me.

340
00:18:08,338 --> 00:18:09,380
Too big.

341
00:18:19,516 --> 00:18:20,683
Why?

342
00:18:21,851 --> 00:18:23,520
I just remembered how when I was a kid,

343
00:18:23,603 --> 00:18:25,021
things were exactly like this!

344
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:27,607
There were a lot of rules,
a lot of orders.

345
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:30,235
She even decided
what clothes I had to wear!

346
00:18:31,402 --> 00:18:33,112
She wasn't looking for a child.

347
00:18:33,613 --> 00:18:34,781
She wanted a doll.

348
00:18:35,365 --> 00:18:36,533
A doll that she could dress up

349
00:18:36,616 --> 00:18:38,910
and that would do everything she wanted.

350
00:18:40,703 --> 00:18:42,914
It was your decision
to work here, wasn't it?

351
00:18:43,706 --> 00:18:44,833
Hm.

352
00:18:44,916 --> 00:18:46,334
Then see it to the end.

353
00:18:52,507 --> 00:18:53,591
Uh…

354
00:18:54,509 --> 00:18:56,094
I can't afford these.

355
00:18:56,511 --> 00:18:57,595
It's fine.

356
00:18:57,679 --> 00:18:59,681
That's one of the benefits
of working here.

357
00:19:01,516 --> 00:19:03,142
Here, wear this.

358
00:19:03,226 --> 00:19:04,477
-Huh?
-Give me your feet.

359
00:19:06,688 --> 00:19:08,231
I know how to wear shoes.

360
00:19:08,481 --> 00:19:10,483
We have so much to do here in the office.

361
00:19:10,817 --> 00:19:12,151
You were even late earlier.

362
00:19:12,902 --> 00:19:14,821
It was just five minutes!

363
00:19:14,904 --> 00:19:16,865
The jeep I was riding in stopped working.

364
00:19:16,948 --> 00:19:18,324
Let me do it.

365
00:19:18,783 --> 00:19:22,245
Do you have any idea how hard it is
to take public transport?

366
00:19:22,704 --> 00:19:24,622
You don't know it because you have a car.

367
00:19:25,373 --> 00:19:26,499
-Your other foot.
-I wonder if your car…

368
00:19:27,417 --> 00:19:29,419
stops working, do you still
not take public transportation?

369
00:19:29,502 --> 00:19:30,795
How do you go to places, then?

370
00:19:31,254 --> 00:19:32,213
Besides, it's impossible.

371
00:19:32,297 --> 00:19:35,508
Have you never been late
in your entire life?

372
00:19:36,217 --> 00:19:37,594
Ah… It's freezing!

373
00:19:37,677 --> 00:19:39,679
-Give me your foot.
-Argh!

374
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:41,598
-The other one.
-Jesus Christ.

375
00:19:46,686 --> 00:19:48,813
First lesson you'll learn in La Familia,

376
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:50,899
there are no excuses.

377
00:19:52,483 --> 00:19:53,818
You can change in the restroom.

378
00:20:00,241 --> 00:20:01,701
Are you okay?

379
00:20:01,784 --> 00:20:02,952
Yes.

380
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:17,800
-Are you okay?
-Mm-hmm.

381
00:20:18,426 --> 00:20:19,469
Here.

382
00:20:19,552 --> 00:20:22,013
That manual contains
all the policies, tasks,

383
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:24,891
and your responsibilities
as an office assistant.

384
00:20:25,183 --> 00:20:27,518
That's why you must memorize that.

385
00:20:27,602 --> 00:20:32,607
But in general, you'll also do
all the errands in the office.

386
00:20:33,316 --> 00:20:35,610
Okay? Let me show you to your desk.

387
00:20:38,947 --> 00:20:40,782
Here's what you asked for, Sir Enzo.

388
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:41,783
Thanks, Sid.

389
00:20:46,412 --> 00:20:47,789
This is my desk?

390
00:20:47,872 --> 00:20:48,998
Looks great.

391
00:20:50,416 --> 00:20:51,584
No.

392
00:20:53,461 --> 00:20:54,629
This is your desk.

393
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:01,135
And this is your first task.

394
00:21:02,971 --> 00:21:05,765
Have all the employees sign
the attendance sheet.

395
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:08,685
When I say everyone, I mean everyone.

396
00:21:09,102 --> 00:21:12,522
From security, utility,
maintenance, etcetera.

397
00:21:12,939 --> 00:21:15,733
From the first floor to the 20th floor.

398
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:20,780
Haven't you heard of biometrics?

399
00:21:21,072 --> 00:21:23,408
Your building looks great,
but it isn't up to date.

400
00:21:23,491 --> 00:21:24,951
Don't you have that here?

401
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:27,120
Ms. D asked for that.

402
00:21:27,912 --> 00:21:29,706
You need to finish it within the day.

403
00:21:29,956 --> 00:21:31,666
Once you're done,
you can report immediately

404
00:21:31,749 --> 00:21:33,918
to the admin manager for your other tasks.

405
00:21:34,627 --> 00:21:35,712
All right?

406
00:21:36,212 --> 00:21:37,422
I'll leave you to it.

407
00:21:37,797 --> 00:21:39,424
-Sir, wait.
-Hmm?

408
00:21:40,550 --> 00:21:42,677
Since you're here, why don't
you sign the attendance sheet?

409
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:53,187
Okay.

410
00:21:53,563 --> 00:21:54,689
Thank you.

411
00:21:55,356 --> 00:21:56,441
Good luck.

412
00:21:59,068 --> 00:21:59,902
AUGUST 3RD 1992

413
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:10,246
Fight, Patricia.

414
00:22:10,788 --> 00:22:14,417
I love my life.

415
00:22:19,172 --> 00:22:21,424
We will be completely
transparent with you.

416
00:22:21,507 --> 00:22:23,134
One thing is for sure,

417
00:22:23,217 --> 00:22:26,971
all your needs will be met.

418
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:30,975
Just like what we did
with the other victims.

419
00:22:31,059 --> 00:22:33,436
I know that you'll silence us with money.

420
00:22:33,519 --> 00:22:34,937
You can't just pay us off!

421
00:22:35,021 --> 00:22:37,815
Just because we are poor
doesn't mean you can step on us.

422
00:22:37,899 --> 00:22:40,318
Right! He's right!

423
00:22:40,401 --> 00:22:43,821
You can't fool everyone
with your promises.

424
00:22:44,238 --> 00:22:45,782
What we want…

425
00:22:46,365 --> 00:22:48,701
is for your boss to pay!

426
00:22:50,703 --> 00:22:53,039
Put Diana Aragon in jail!

427
00:22:53,122 --> 00:22:54,707
Put her in jail!

428
00:22:54,791 --> 00:23:00,254
Put Diana Aragon in jail!

429
00:23:01,339 --> 00:23:01,964
A FAMILY IS COMPLETE WITH CALA SODA

430
00:23:02,048 --> 00:23:03,049
Tenth floor.

431
00:23:03,132 --> 00:23:05,593
Accounting and Finance.

432
00:23:05,927 --> 00:23:06,969
Ah.

433
00:23:07,637 --> 00:23:09,430
-Sir Joseph Vargas?
-Ah, yes?

434
00:23:09,514 --> 00:23:11,307
Please sign the attendance sheet.

435
00:23:11,390 --> 00:23:12,225
Ah, yes.

436
00:23:12,308 --> 00:23:15,561
So you're the one going around
to get the attendance.

437
00:23:15,978 --> 00:23:17,021
Ah, yes.

438
00:23:17,105 --> 00:23:19,107
There are a lot of employees here.

439
00:23:19,982 --> 00:23:21,818
I already went to three floors.

440
00:23:21,901 --> 00:23:22,819
I have five left.

441
00:23:27,573 --> 00:23:28,699
Ah! I'm so sorry.

442
00:23:28,783 --> 00:23:31,661
I'm so sorry, but could you
please sign the attendance?

443
00:23:31,953 --> 00:23:33,079
I'm sorry.

444
00:23:35,873 --> 00:23:37,792
Ah… Marco Majes, right?

445
00:23:37,875 --> 00:23:39,377
Could you sign as well?

446
00:23:39,627 --> 00:23:42,547
Please wash your hands before you sign.

447
00:23:49,303 --> 00:23:50,888
You're the new office assistant, right?

448
00:23:50,972 --> 00:23:52,014
-Yes.
-Well…

449
00:23:52,098 --> 00:23:53,641
this is needed on the eighth floor.

450
00:23:54,225 --> 00:23:55,977
Could you please hand this over to them?

451
00:23:56,269 --> 00:23:58,479
-If it's okay?
-Yes, of course!

452
00:23:59,397 --> 00:24:00,982
How's the meeting earlier?

453
00:24:01,065 --> 00:24:02,984
Hold on. Where are you heading?

454
00:24:04,152 --> 00:24:07,113
Kidding. Before you leave
could you sign this for me?

455
00:24:15,121 --> 00:24:16,080
Please sign this.

456
00:24:20,209 --> 00:24:21,752
Thank you.

457
00:24:27,967 --> 00:24:29,844
Hello? Yes.

458
00:24:30,887 --> 00:24:33,764
We were talking to your staff earlier.

459
00:24:35,850 --> 00:24:38,144
They want to settle.

460
00:24:38,227 --> 00:24:40,396
I already convinced my companions

461
00:24:40,479 --> 00:24:42,732
to refuse, just like you said.

462
00:24:44,108 --> 00:24:46,194
How long will we refuse to settle?

463
00:24:47,195 --> 00:24:49,906
Their offer for damages is quite large.

464
00:24:49,989 --> 00:24:51,199
Hold on.

465
00:24:51,824 --> 00:24:53,576
Aren't they your co-workers?

466
00:24:54,493 --> 00:24:56,537
This might lead to an investigation,
I don't want to get in trouble.

467
00:24:57,455 --> 00:25:00,082
Hey! What are you doing here?

468
00:25:01,918 --> 00:25:04,253
Um… I'm just getting some air.

469
00:25:05,254 --> 00:25:06,255
What about you?

470
00:25:08,216 --> 00:25:09,508
Nothing.

471
00:25:12,345 --> 00:25:15,473
Aren't you with
La Familia's lawyers earlier?

472
00:25:16,933 --> 00:25:18,392
Your watch looks nice.

473
00:25:19,310 --> 00:25:21,062
Looks expensive.

474
00:25:21,145 --> 00:25:23,314
I got this for a low price.
And besides, it's fake.

475
00:25:25,149 --> 00:25:27,652
And your phone,
that's the new model, right?

476
00:25:27,735 --> 00:25:30,196
-I wanted to get that.
-Then do it.

477
00:25:30,279 --> 00:25:31,489
What do I care?

478
00:25:42,083 --> 00:25:45,253
I need the new draft
on administrative process by tomorrow.

479
00:25:45,336 --> 00:25:46,337
Yes, ma'am.

480
00:26:07,191 --> 00:26:08,484
Here's what you asked for.

481
00:26:13,197 --> 00:26:16,993
When I said I wanted everyone's signature,

482
00:26:17,660 --> 00:26:23,624
I expected everyone, including those
in the janitorial services department.

483
00:26:24,667 --> 00:26:25,751
Excuse me, ma'am.

484
00:26:29,005 --> 00:26:30,089
This is complete.

485
00:26:31,382 --> 00:26:34,552
I actually found so much about them.

486
00:26:34,635 --> 00:26:36,512
You still have a lot of things to do.

487
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:38,597
Just wait for further instructions.

488
00:26:39,015 --> 00:26:40,141
Yes, ma'am.

489
00:26:40,224 --> 00:26:41,309
Ms. D.

490
00:26:43,352 --> 00:26:44,854
About the rally…

491
00:26:44,937 --> 00:26:46,355
they're still out there.

492
00:26:46,689 --> 00:26:48,774
They don't want to accept the offers.

493
00:26:48,858 --> 00:26:50,901
Didn't I tell you
to offer something higher?

494
00:26:50,985 --> 00:26:52,820
Make it double or even triple!

495
00:26:53,612 --> 00:26:54,739
Noted, Ms. D.

496
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:00,202
Is there something funny?

497
00:27:03,622 --> 00:27:06,751
I thought that maybe
that's not what they need.

498
00:27:07,001 --> 00:27:08,586
When people are in need,

499
00:27:08,669 --> 00:27:10,546
they are desperate for someone to talk to.

500
00:27:10,629 --> 00:27:12,465
Do you think it's that easy?

501
00:27:13,591 --> 00:27:15,468
You don't know what's at stake here.

502
00:27:15,926 --> 00:27:18,179
What they've been through isn't a joke.

503
00:27:19,221 --> 00:27:21,098
I was just thinking about the victims.

504
00:27:21,557 --> 00:27:22,725
Me too.

505
00:27:23,309 --> 00:27:26,312
That's why I'm making sure
that there is still a company standing

506
00:27:26,729 --> 00:27:29,774
who'll take accountability
and will help them.

507
00:27:32,318 --> 00:27:34,236
This is just your first day here,

508
00:27:34,612 --> 00:27:36,280
you think you know everything.

509
00:27:37,031 --> 00:27:39,825
You think you know better than us

510
00:27:40,159 --> 00:27:42,119
who has worked for decades

511
00:27:42,328 --> 00:27:44,914
who worked very hard
to keep this company afloat.

512
00:27:57,968 --> 00:28:01,180
Please make room
so you won't get dispersed.

513
00:28:01,263 --> 00:28:03,391
And so you won't disrupt their work.

514
00:28:05,643 --> 00:28:06,852
Please move.

515
00:28:06,936 --> 00:28:08,229
We need to talk to someone, sir.

516
00:28:12,191 --> 00:28:13,025
You're bothering the workers.

517
00:28:13,109 --> 00:28:14,985
-We're rallying.
-We need help, sir!

518
00:28:15,069 --> 00:28:17,321
We just need someone to hear us out.

519
00:28:38,217 --> 00:28:40,511
Bugoy! Son!

520
00:28:41,887 --> 00:28:43,973
Bugoy, are you hurt?

521
00:28:44,056 --> 00:28:46,934
I told you not to stray far from me.

522
00:28:47,017 --> 00:28:49,186
-He… He's fine.
-Does it hurt?

523
00:28:49,270 --> 00:28:51,230
He's fine, don't get mad at him.

524
00:28:51,313 --> 00:28:53,607
Thank you. Thank you very much.

525
00:28:54,066 --> 00:28:57,403
Ah… what's your name?

526
00:28:58,028 --> 00:29:00,156
Rosenda. My name is Rosenda.

527
00:29:00,781 --> 00:29:02,450
My name is Patricia.

528
00:29:04,285 --> 00:29:05,828
Can I talk to you in private?

529
00:29:06,245 --> 00:29:08,080
I work for La Familia.

530
00:29:08,831 --> 00:29:12,001
I am not the one you should be talking to.

531
00:29:12,084 --> 00:29:14,628
You should talk to Carlo. He's our leader.

532
00:29:15,504 --> 00:29:18,007
I want to talk to the mothers.

533
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:21,594
I want to know why
you won't settle with us.

534
00:29:25,431 --> 00:29:28,517
We really didn't want
to blow the issue up anymore.

535
00:29:29,685 --> 00:29:33,898
The lawyer of La Familia
already talked to us.

536
00:29:34,899 --> 00:29:36,066
But…

537
00:29:36,567 --> 00:29:37,943
Carlo didn't like it.

538
00:29:38,402 --> 00:29:39,528
He said it wasn't enough.

539
00:29:39,612 --> 00:29:41,447
He said that we should file a complaint.

540
00:29:43,199 --> 00:29:46,952
He said that if we caused more trouble,
they'll offer something bigger.

541
00:29:47,995 --> 00:29:51,499
That's right.
That's why we should talk to Carlo

542
00:29:51,582 --> 00:29:53,501
because he's the one stopping us.

543
00:29:55,920 --> 00:29:57,129
Is that so?

544
00:29:57,838 --> 00:29:59,632
Carlo has a point.

545
00:30:00,049 --> 00:30:02,885
What my son has been through isn't easy.

546
00:30:02,968 --> 00:30:05,221
And besides, this isn't just about money.

547
00:30:08,182 --> 00:30:12,728
When my son got poisoned,
I didn't know what to do.

548
00:30:12,811 --> 00:30:15,606
You'll understand
once you become a mother.

549
00:30:15,898 --> 00:30:17,566
Every mother is like this.

550
00:30:19,193 --> 00:30:22,613
I hope you understand our situation.

551
00:30:22,696 --> 00:30:24,240
Trust me.

552
00:30:25,241 --> 00:30:27,368
I understand you all.

553
00:30:27,451 --> 00:30:29,578
I understand you, Rosenda.

554
00:30:29,828 --> 00:30:31,038
But…

555
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:34,583
it doesn't have to get this messy, right?

556
00:30:34,917 --> 00:30:37,044
We are ready to listen to you.

557
00:30:37,127 --> 00:30:38,712
La Familia is ready to listen to you.

558
00:30:38,963 --> 00:30:41,340
Why don't you talk to Carlo about this?

559
00:30:43,133 --> 00:30:44,510
Rosenda.

560
00:30:45,553 --> 00:30:47,304
As you said earlier…

561
00:30:48,264 --> 00:30:49,557
you are a mother.

562
00:30:51,267 --> 00:30:54,228
You are the ones
who understand the situation best.

563
00:30:55,229 --> 00:30:58,232
There are a lot of children affected.

564
00:30:59,149 --> 00:31:02,319
So please, allow me to help you.

565
00:31:03,487 --> 00:31:05,739
That's why I wanted to talk to you.

566
00:31:05,990 --> 00:31:09,577
Help me convince the mothers
who are with you.

567
00:31:12,162 --> 00:31:14,248
There's a way for this to be settled.

568
00:31:15,291 --> 00:31:16,875
What have you thought of?

569
00:31:23,382 --> 00:31:27,386
Miss, where's Patricia's office?

570
00:31:27,469 --> 00:31:31,015
The owner's daughter.
He's the father of the owner's daughter.

571
00:31:31,307 --> 00:31:33,017
Right there, sir.

572
00:31:34,560 --> 00:31:36,437
Give us a cup of coffee later.

573
00:31:37,146 --> 00:31:38,939
Hurry with that, okay?

574
00:31:41,900 --> 00:31:43,277
Ah, miss?

575
00:31:43,777 --> 00:31:46,363
Is this Patricia's office?

576
00:31:46,447 --> 00:31:49,491
This space doesn't seem quite right

577
00:31:49,575 --> 00:31:51,994
for the owner's daughter's office.

578
00:31:52,077 --> 00:31:53,203
Oh, no.

579
00:31:53,287 --> 00:31:54,580
That's actually her table.

580
00:31:54,663 --> 00:31:56,415
She's our new assistant.

581
00:31:57,041 --> 00:31:58,083
If you'll excuse me.

582
00:32:03,839 --> 00:32:05,090
This is her office?

583
00:32:05,758 --> 00:32:08,135
This is where she put Patricia?

584
00:32:10,262 --> 00:32:11,889
-Yes.
-Look.

585
00:32:12,556 --> 00:32:15,309
Look at what she's done to our daughter.

586
00:32:22,858 --> 00:32:23,901
Sir.

587
00:32:23,984 --> 00:32:25,903
Based on the preliminary results,

588
00:32:25,986 --> 00:32:27,780
it does not appear to be an accident.

589
00:32:31,367 --> 00:32:32,660
It was intentional?

590
00:32:33,410 --> 00:32:35,579
Here. Take a look, sir.

591
00:32:36,914 --> 00:32:40,376
There is no trace of contamination
on the other soda batches.

592
00:32:40,668 --> 00:32:42,127
But everyone who got sick,

593
00:32:42,378 --> 00:32:44,380
came from the feeding
program distribution.

594
00:32:44,463 --> 00:32:45,923
So it was done on a specific channel.

595
00:32:46,173 --> 00:32:48,217
-Oh, I'm sorry.
-It seems targeted.

596
00:32:52,096 --> 00:32:53,263
What is this?

597
00:32:56,850 --> 00:32:58,352
This is an internal investigation.

598
00:33:00,270 --> 00:33:02,564
-Teddy.
-That's Mr. Aragon to you.

599
00:33:03,899 --> 00:33:05,442
Is this part of your job?

600
00:33:06,985 --> 00:33:09,780
In order to fix something broken,

601
00:33:10,322 --> 00:33:12,157
I need to know how it broke.

602
00:33:12,825 --> 00:33:14,326
I'm just doing my job.

603
00:33:15,786 --> 00:33:18,747
Are there some things
that I shouldn't know?

604
00:33:19,123 --> 00:33:20,457
What exactly

605
00:33:21,458 --> 00:33:22,793
are you trying to say?

606
00:33:25,129 --> 00:33:28,340
Ms. D, Patricia is talking
to the victims downstairs.

607
00:33:28,424 --> 00:33:29,550
What?

608
00:33:29,633 --> 00:33:30,801
Who told her to do that?

609
00:33:31,135 --> 00:33:32,344
Ms. D!

610
00:33:34,138 --> 00:33:35,431
I have something to tell you.

611
00:33:35,723 --> 00:33:37,850
Why are you meddling in things

612
00:33:37,933 --> 00:33:39,560
that have nothing to do
with your scope of work?

613
00:33:39,810 --> 00:33:40,811
What?

614
00:33:40,894 --> 00:33:42,146
You're unbelievable!

615
00:33:42,229 --> 00:33:44,565
Why are you talking to the victims?

616
00:33:44,940 --> 00:33:47,151
-Who told you to do that?
-Diana!

617
00:33:47,776 --> 00:33:49,486
Why are you yelling at my daughter?

618
00:33:50,112 --> 00:33:51,864
You have no right
to talk to her like that.

619
00:33:51,947 --> 00:33:54,032
And what are you doing here?

620
00:33:54,450 --> 00:33:55,993
Visiting her.

621
00:33:56,535 --> 00:33:58,162
Thankfully, I did. Because if I didn't,

622
00:33:58,412 --> 00:34:01,206
I wouldn't know that
you would treat her this way.

623
00:34:01,290 --> 00:34:04,460
Of course, you're freaking out
without knowing anything.

624
00:34:04,793 --> 00:34:07,504
I was reprimanding her
because she did something wrong.

625
00:34:07,588 --> 00:34:09,047
She's not trained for that.

626
00:34:09,131 --> 00:34:10,549
What if she got in danger?

627
00:34:10,632 --> 00:34:14,303
What if she said something
to harm the company?

628
00:34:14,386 --> 00:34:18,015
Do you even understand the legal risks?

629
00:34:18,098 --> 00:34:20,809
Until now, is that what you think of me?

630
00:34:21,185 --> 00:34:22,978
I talked to them because

631
00:34:23,437 --> 00:34:26,398
they needed someone to talk to.

632
00:34:27,441 --> 00:34:28,609
I'm sorry.

633
00:34:29,276 --> 00:34:31,528
I thought I was helping.

634
00:34:32,821 --> 00:34:37,159
Here's a list of those willing
to negotiate for a settlement.

635
00:34:37,659 --> 00:34:41,246
Those who were opposed to it
are open and waiting now.

636
00:34:41,622 --> 00:34:42,956
See?

637
00:34:43,832 --> 00:34:46,293
You should be thankful, Diana.

638
00:34:46,376 --> 00:34:48,128
No, that is not the point.

639
00:34:49,254 --> 00:34:52,132
You do not make decisions
on your own, Patricia.

640
00:34:52,591 --> 00:34:54,676
We have a protocol to follow.

641
00:34:55,219 --> 00:35:00,015
What you've done out there
with no clearance,

642
00:35:00,098 --> 00:35:02,518
that can put the whole company at risk.

643
00:35:02,768 --> 00:35:06,313
Just say you're mad at Patricia!

644
00:35:06,396 --> 00:35:08,524
We saw the desk you assigned her in.

645
00:35:08,607 --> 00:35:11,443
-You put her in a small…
-Quit butting in.

646
00:35:11,527 --> 00:35:14,488
Is that how little you think of Patricia?

647
00:35:14,571 --> 00:35:16,907
I don't need to explain anything to you.

648
00:35:17,324 --> 00:35:20,035
But for the sake of your peace of mind,

649
00:35:20,118 --> 00:35:22,329
I assigned her as an office assistant

650
00:35:22,412 --> 00:35:24,248
so she can learn.

651
00:35:24,331 --> 00:35:26,750
She's an honor student!

652
00:35:27,251 --> 00:35:28,794
She also has a scholarship!

653
00:35:29,044 --> 00:35:30,712
But she stopped studying at some point.

654
00:35:30,796 --> 00:35:32,881
You did the same thing to me before.

655
00:35:33,382 --> 00:35:35,092
You're pulling me down

656
00:35:35,175 --> 00:35:36,677
because you want to be
the only one at the top!

657
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:39,096
-That's enough.
-Now I see it.

658
00:35:39,179 --> 00:35:41,431
This conversation isn't about Patricia.

659
00:35:41,515 --> 00:35:42,808
It's about you.

660
00:35:43,267 --> 00:35:47,062
Because until now,
your ego is still bruised.

661
00:35:47,479 --> 00:35:48,939
What do you want me to do?

662
00:35:49,398 --> 00:35:53,569
Just let her sit there all day,
just like what you did before?

663
00:35:53,652 --> 00:35:57,197
Like a worthless nepo husband?

664
00:35:57,281 --> 00:36:01,285
Using the Aragon name as you please?

665
00:36:01,368 --> 00:36:04,037
Thank goodness
she didn't grow up with you!

666
00:36:04,246 --> 00:36:06,415
Because if she did,
she'd end up just like you!

667
00:36:06,498 --> 00:36:07,875
-Boss?
-Pa, that's enough.

668
00:36:07,958 --> 00:36:09,877
What you're doing doesn't seem right.

669
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:11,795
-Calm down.
-And who are you?

670
00:36:12,671 --> 00:36:14,506
You are not part of our conversation!

671
00:36:14,590 --> 00:36:16,049
Don't get involved!

672
00:36:16,133 --> 00:36:17,509
You aren't talking.

673
00:36:18,135 --> 00:36:20,512
You're causing a scandal.
If you continue this,

674
00:36:20,888 --> 00:36:23,181
we'll sue you for Unjust Vexation,

675
00:36:23,849 --> 00:36:26,018
Grave Threats and Trespassing.

676
00:36:26,268 --> 00:36:28,186
Wait a minute.

677
00:36:29,563 --> 00:36:31,315
There's no need to take it that far.

678
00:36:31,398 --> 00:36:33,233
My family will leave peacefully.

679
00:36:34,276 --> 00:36:35,319
Pa?

680
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,824
You'll go down one day, Diana.

681
00:36:43,327 --> 00:36:44,620
You'll get what's coming to you.

682
00:36:50,792 --> 00:36:54,504
If you can't respect me in my own company,

683
00:36:55,297 --> 00:36:56,340
leave.

684
00:36:57,257 --> 00:36:59,468
Leave my company now!

685
00:37:00,260 --> 00:37:01,303
Get out!

686
00:37:05,057 --> 00:37:06,767
Come with us, Patricia.

687
00:37:08,602 --> 00:37:10,979
You don't need to put up with this hell.

688
00:37:16,276 --> 00:37:17,569
Patricia.

689
00:37:24,660 --> 00:37:25,827
Here's the list of people.

690
00:37:52,062 --> 00:37:53,271
Are you okay?

691
00:37:55,148 --> 00:37:56,358
I'm fine.

692
00:37:59,653 --> 00:38:02,364
Would you like me
to solve the problem with your husband?

693
00:38:05,534 --> 00:38:07,411
You can't destroy his life.

694
00:38:08,120 --> 00:38:09,955
He did it on his own.

695
00:38:10,414 --> 00:38:12,249
That's not part of your job.

696
00:38:12,708 --> 00:38:14,626
This is my personal life.

697
00:38:14,710 --> 00:38:15,919
Diana…

698
00:38:16,878 --> 00:38:18,714
you are La Familia.

699
00:38:19,631 --> 00:38:22,300
Your personal life
is part of the business.

700
00:38:22,843 --> 00:38:24,219
And part of my job…

701
00:38:25,762 --> 00:38:27,305
is to find out the SWOT.

702
00:38:28,682 --> 00:38:30,434
Strengths, weaknesses,

703
00:38:31,268 --> 00:38:33,895
opportunities,
and most importantly, threats.

704
00:38:34,187 --> 00:38:36,440
I need to know who isn't right for you.

705
00:38:37,107 --> 00:38:39,192
I need to know
who's ruining and hurting you.

706
00:38:42,779 --> 00:38:45,365
Martin can't do anything to hurt me again.

707
00:38:46,908 --> 00:38:50,287
You know I caught him cheating on me
with my best friend.

708
00:38:51,747 --> 00:38:54,416
Carlota, who was my former secretary.

709
00:38:55,208 --> 00:38:56,293
Does Patricia know?

710
00:38:57,127 --> 00:38:58,920
I wouldn't stoop so low

711
00:38:59,880 --> 00:39:02,132
as to destroy her father

712
00:39:02,215 --> 00:39:04,885
just to prove my point to my child.

713
00:39:05,802 --> 00:39:07,387
I won't stoop that low.

714
00:39:07,804 --> 00:39:11,308
I'm nothing like Martin,
who has to tear others down

715
00:39:11,683 --> 00:39:13,310
to prove that I'm right.

716
00:39:13,393 --> 00:39:17,814
If we hadn't gone there,
then we wouldn't have seen her.

717
00:39:17,898 --> 00:39:20,192
Now my day's ruined.

718
00:39:21,109 --> 00:39:23,487
Why did it have to get
to the point of arguing again?

719
00:39:23,945 --> 00:39:25,822
Patricia, the reason I came to your office

720
00:39:25,906 --> 00:39:27,574
is because I'm proud of you.

721
00:39:28,158 --> 00:39:30,410
Because it's your first day at your job.

722
00:39:30,619 --> 00:39:32,412
And who wouldn't get mad at that Diana

723
00:39:32,496 --> 00:39:34,623
when she treats you so badly?

724
00:39:34,706 --> 00:39:39,044
You're the daughter of the owner
yet she mistreats you just like that?

725
00:39:39,127 --> 00:39:40,462
You know what…

726
00:39:40,962 --> 00:39:42,589
Diana just wants to get back at you

727
00:39:42,672 --> 00:39:44,716
because you didn't choose her back then.

728
00:39:44,966 --> 00:39:46,384
Why did you marry him?

729
00:39:48,762 --> 00:39:50,138
Because I thought…

730
00:39:52,224 --> 00:39:54,935
he's the only one who knew…

731
00:39:55,143 --> 00:39:56,144
the real me…

732
00:39:56,394 --> 00:39:58,438
outside of this status,

733
00:39:58,814 --> 00:40:01,650
who would love me completely.

734
00:40:06,279 --> 00:40:08,406
When we were about to marry, I thought,

735
00:40:10,075 --> 00:40:11,952
I would have everything.

736
00:40:12,786 --> 00:40:14,412
The one time…

737
00:40:15,163 --> 00:40:17,541
I disobeyed my Papa…

738
00:40:20,460 --> 00:40:22,629
turned out to cause me
the most harm of all.

739
00:40:24,089 --> 00:40:27,008
As my position in the company
continued to rise higher,

740
00:40:27,551 --> 00:40:29,678
Martin's ego couldn't accept it.

741
00:40:30,345 --> 00:40:33,598
So he never missed any chance…

742
00:40:34,391 --> 00:40:38,353
to make me feel like I wasn't good enough.

743
00:40:41,648 --> 00:40:43,275
That's how much of an idiot I am.

744
00:40:47,946 --> 00:40:49,281
I don't think so.

745
00:40:49,364 --> 00:40:50,657
Maybe naive.

746
00:40:56,079 --> 00:40:59,916
You know, he even turned
my own daughter against me.

747
00:41:05,213 --> 00:41:06,631
Get back to work.

748
00:41:07,716 --> 00:41:09,009
Visit the victims.

749
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:12,262
Find out if what Patricia
is saying is true.

750
00:41:13,471 --> 00:41:14,472
Yes, ma'am.

751
00:41:19,477 --> 00:41:21,813
But it's not right
to just barge in carelessly!

752
00:41:21,897 --> 00:41:23,356
Wait a minute, Patricia.

753
00:41:23,440 --> 00:41:25,734
Your father is just defending you,

754
00:41:25,817 --> 00:41:27,444
now it's as if he's the bad guy.

755
00:41:27,527 --> 00:41:29,863
Because you don't have to defend me.

756
00:41:29,946 --> 00:41:31,323
I can handle things on my own!

757
00:41:31,698 --> 00:41:33,491
And I'm happy with the job she's given me.

758
00:41:33,575 --> 00:41:36,703
What's important for me
is I have a regular income.

759
00:41:36,786 --> 00:41:38,997
So you are on Diana's side

760
00:41:39,080 --> 00:41:41,082
-over your father's, huh?
-That's not it.

761
00:41:41,166 --> 00:41:43,043
You don't understand
where I'm coming from.

762
00:41:43,501 --> 00:41:45,921
What, now we're too dumb to get you?

763
00:41:46,004 --> 00:41:47,839
-That's not it!
-That's enough!

764
00:41:48,965 --> 00:41:51,843
Before you get mistreated in that company,

765
00:41:52,344 --> 00:41:53,678
you better resign now.

766
00:41:54,137 --> 00:41:58,767
I won't allow Diana to make you suffer
just to get back at me.

767
00:41:59,392 --> 00:42:00,727
You should resign.

768
00:42:30,090 --> 00:42:32,592
Diana, you are meant

769
00:42:32,676 --> 00:42:33,718
-to lead La Familia.
-Papa!

770
00:42:37,264 --> 00:42:38,515
So…

771
00:42:39,849 --> 00:42:42,477
Um, here's the attendance sheet.

772
00:42:42,852 --> 00:42:45,855
It's complete with all
of the employees' signatures.

773
00:42:45,939 --> 00:42:49,734
Well, looks like I'm going to talk to HR

774
00:42:49,818 --> 00:42:53,071
to inform them about your…
summer job here.

775
00:42:53,446 --> 00:42:57,492
Consider this
as your early practicum for the company.

776
00:42:57,575 --> 00:42:58,827
And at the same time,

777
00:42:59,286 --> 00:43:02,122
this will give you an advantage
when you step into college.

778
00:43:02,497 --> 00:43:04,082
I want you to learn…

779
00:43:04,332 --> 00:43:07,919
how to manage a business.

780
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:12,340
I hope you understand why I'm doing this.

781
00:43:12,424 --> 00:43:15,051
So that I could know
the company's staff better.

782
00:43:16,052 --> 00:43:18,054
And for me to realize the responsibilities

783
00:43:18,138 --> 00:43:19,889
and importance of each one of them.

784
00:43:20,515 --> 00:43:21,933
I hope you don't disappoint me.

785
00:43:22,892 --> 00:43:24,060
I'll do my best.

786
00:43:36,072 --> 00:43:37,782
Good morning, Ms. D, Sir Teddy.

787
00:43:39,326 --> 00:43:41,286
Patricia hasn't come in yet.

788
00:43:46,458 --> 00:43:48,668
Just accept it, Sis.

789
00:43:49,044 --> 00:43:52,172
Kids these days are too sensitive.

790
00:43:52,255 --> 00:43:55,467
Give them a little challenge
and they'll give up right away.

791
00:44:05,518 --> 00:44:06,770
Good morning, Ms. D.

792
00:44:12,567 --> 00:44:14,569
I thought you're never coming back.

793
00:44:15,111 --> 00:44:17,155
I know how to follow through
with my words.

794
00:44:17,238 --> 00:44:18,907
Your payment to me is still not settled.

795
00:44:18,990 --> 00:44:20,408
Once it does I'll leave.

796
00:44:21,284 --> 00:44:23,286
And you'll never see me ever again.

797
00:44:26,790 --> 00:44:28,792
But I can say with my whole heart

798
00:44:28,875 --> 00:44:30,460
that I didn't do anything wrong.

799
00:44:33,129 --> 00:44:36,299
About what my father did…

800
00:44:37,675 --> 00:44:39,344
I already talked to him. I apologize.

801
00:44:39,427 --> 00:44:40,804
No.

802
00:44:41,388 --> 00:44:44,099
Don't apologize for him.

803
00:44:44,974 --> 00:44:46,017
Okay?

804
00:44:52,732 --> 00:44:53,983
Yes?

805
00:44:54,859 --> 00:44:56,945
Do you not have anything to say to me?

806
00:44:57,028 --> 00:44:59,239
I would've already did if there was any.

807
00:45:03,493 --> 00:45:04,661
You're, um…

808
00:45:06,162 --> 00:45:08,123
wearing comfortable shoes today.

809
00:45:11,418 --> 00:45:13,128
-I brought the heels with me.
-Oh.

810
00:45:13,211 --> 00:45:14,921
-I'll wear it in a bit.
-No need.

811
00:45:15,004 --> 00:45:16,381
You're late.

812
00:45:16,798 --> 00:45:20,343
Just finish the things I've told you
to do yesterday.

813
00:45:20,427 --> 00:45:22,929
And then, go to the factory.

814
00:45:23,179 --> 00:45:25,306
I want you to collect all of the reports

815
00:45:25,390 --> 00:45:28,101
from the assembly line
and the logistics there, okay?

816
00:45:31,187 --> 00:45:32,564
I'll change into my heels.

817
00:45:46,911 --> 00:45:48,997
I heard about what happened yesterday.

818
00:45:50,039 --> 00:45:52,208
Uncle Martin is just awful, Dad.

819
00:45:53,626 --> 00:45:56,629
Diana and Patricia can't reconcile.

820
00:45:57,255 --> 00:45:59,048
Because when that happens,

821
00:45:59,424 --> 00:46:02,177
she'll groom Patricia
to become her successor.

822
00:46:02,802 --> 00:46:04,512
And we'll be out of the picture.

823
00:46:05,472 --> 00:46:07,223
Not just in the picture.

824
00:46:11,227 --> 00:46:13,062
We will lose everything.

825
00:46:18,109 --> 00:46:19,027
Take the initiative.

826
00:46:19,110 --> 00:46:20,487
-Get those files now.
-Yes, sir. I'll get them.

827
00:46:20,570 --> 00:46:22,071
-Please, hurry.
-I'll bring them now.

828
00:46:22,155 --> 00:46:23,698
-Yes, sir.
-Hey.

829
00:46:24,782 --> 00:46:26,534
-What?
-Why were you running off

830
00:46:26,618 --> 00:46:28,286
-your mouth yesterday?
-What?

831
00:46:28,620 --> 00:46:31,331
Hey, I had no bad intentions.

832
00:46:32,248 --> 00:46:34,834
I merely just said what I saw.

833
00:46:34,918 --> 00:46:37,337
And Ms. D wants to know everything.

834
00:46:38,004 --> 00:46:39,506
I didn't say anything wrong, okay?

835
00:46:39,589 --> 00:46:41,174
-I had no bad intentions.
-Really?

836
00:46:41,257 --> 00:46:43,343
I don't know what you
talked about with the victims.

837
00:46:43,426 --> 00:46:45,345
You don't know? So you didn't
hear it and made things up?

838
00:46:45,428 --> 00:46:46,888
I didn't make things up.

839
00:46:47,305 --> 00:46:50,391
All I said was that I saw you
with the people from the rally.

840
00:46:50,475 --> 00:46:51,518
That's all!

841
00:46:51,601 --> 00:46:54,729
Okay? I didn't know that Ms. D
would think of it differently.

842
00:46:56,022 --> 00:46:58,149
I helped them out but I ended up
looking like the bad person.

843
00:46:59,484 --> 00:47:00,944
You're just like them, aren't you?

844
00:47:01,194 --> 00:47:02,612
You want me out.

845
00:47:05,949 --> 00:47:07,075
It… It's not like that, Patricia.

846
00:47:07,158 --> 00:47:09,702
-I, uh…
-Sir, here are the files.

847
00:47:12,455 --> 00:47:13,414
Blabbermouth.

848
00:47:16,292 --> 00:47:18,336
-Sir.
-It's all good. Go ahead.

849
00:47:20,713 --> 00:47:22,048
Signed waivers.

850
00:47:24,592 --> 00:47:28,429
The victims Patricia talked to
agreed to the settlement.

851
00:47:29,264 --> 00:47:32,225
You know what, Diana, Patricia is useful.

852
00:47:32,517 --> 00:47:33,977
That kid's excellent.

853
00:47:36,271 --> 00:47:38,439
They didn't just hear
her talk about money.

854
00:47:39,941 --> 00:47:41,859
There's sincerity, empathy.

855
00:47:42,986 --> 00:47:44,070
For the first time,

856
00:47:44,153 --> 00:47:46,281
someone really listened to them.

857
00:47:47,031 --> 00:47:48,366
With this development,

858
00:47:48,449 --> 00:47:51,452
maybe we'd be able
to convince Burger City International

859
00:47:51,536 --> 00:47:52,996
to push through with the partnership.

860
00:47:53,663 --> 00:47:55,373
Did Patricia convince all of them?

861
00:47:55,456 --> 00:47:57,458
There's still a few
who's stubborn about it.

862
00:47:57,542 --> 00:48:00,628
There's a faction of the victims
that didn't sign.

863
00:48:01,170 --> 00:48:03,673
And they're not acting
like ordinary victims.

864
00:48:04,215 --> 00:48:05,550
What do you mean?

865
00:48:06,134 --> 00:48:09,429
It seems like something's inciting them
to reject the settlement.

866
00:48:09,679 --> 00:48:11,973
It seems like they don't just want
a simple compensation.

867
00:48:12,390 --> 00:48:14,392
It's like they want to knock you down.

868
00:48:14,851 --> 00:48:15,935
I'm sorry for interrupting.

869
00:48:16,019 --> 00:48:18,021
-What is it?
-Ms. D, you need to see this.

870
00:48:18,438 --> 00:48:20,273
A new video is circulating.

871
00:48:20,690 --> 00:48:22,859
Do you know one of the most controversial

872
00:48:22,942 --> 00:48:24,485
things to happen at La Familia?

873
00:48:25,820 --> 00:48:27,655
The huge fire incident from then…

874
00:48:27,864 --> 00:48:30,033
that is still unsolved today.

875
00:48:31,159 --> 00:48:34,203
It's possible that Diana Aragon
has something to do with it.

876
00:48:35,496 --> 00:48:37,415
The tragedy at La Familia…

877
00:48:37,498 --> 00:48:39,208
What is this nonsense?

878
00:48:41,711 --> 00:48:44,797
or was it a ploy
to save a failing company?

879
00:48:44,881 --> 00:48:47,508
But based on the official investigation,

880
00:48:47,884 --> 00:48:50,136
there was one person singled out
to be the perpetrator.

881
00:48:50,219 --> 00:48:51,971
Cecilia Pineda.

882
00:48:52,055 --> 00:48:54,641
The question is, why her?

883
00:48:54,724 --> 00:48:57,769
Did they use her to cover up
for the real culprit?

884
00:49:01,397 --> 00:49:04,651
Or did the Aragon family
completely silence her?

885
00:49:04,984 --> 00:49:06,402
According to the record,

886
00:49:06,486 --> 00:49:08,655
Patricia gave out a statement,

887
00:49:08,738 --> 00:49:10,948
who was only eight years old at the time.

888
00:49:11,032 --> 00:49:13,242
She heard that her grandfather
and her mother

889
00:49:13,326 --> 00:49:14,827
were involved in the incident.

890
00:49:16,120 --> 00:49:19,666
Is the saying
that children don't lie, true?

891
00:49:19,749 --> 00:49:21,000
Could this have caused

892
00:49:21,084 --> 00:49:23,586
the rift between the mother and daughter?

893
00:49:24,545 --> 00:49:26,798
Who posted this garbage?

894
00:49:27,423 --> 00:49:28,966
It's just a new account, Ms. D.

895
00:49:29,509 --> 00:49:32,595
Find out where this came from.

896
00:49:32,679 --> 00:49:34,931
And do everything you can
to get rid of it.

897
00:49:35,515 --> 00:49:36,849
Yes, Ms. D.

898
00:49:44,816 --> 00:49:47,276
Let's meet in the training room
in 15 minutes.

899
00:49:47,360 --> 00:49:50,446
I'll teach you everything
you need to do here there.

900
00:49:50,863 --> 00:49:52,365
After the briefing,

901
00:49:52,448 --> 00:49:54,075
I'll give you a tour of the factory.

902
00:49:55,118 --> 00:49:56,828
-Okay.
-I'll get going then.

903
00:50:36,075 --> 00:50:38,119
Have you seen
that trending AI generated video

904
00:50:38,619 --> 00:50:40,747
about the La Familia fire?

905
00:50:41,289 --> 00:50:43,624
I did. It's fake news.

906
00:50:43,708 --> 00:50:45,626
Why did they do it?

907
00:50:45,710 --> 00:50:47,587
For the insurance.

908
00:50:47,670 --> 00:50:49,088
Uh, excuse me!

909
00:50:50,006 --> 00:50:52,049
What AI generated video
of La Familia was it?

910
00:50:52,633 --> 00:50:53,801
-Uh, here.
-…things to happen

911
00:50:53,885 --> 00:50:54,802
at La Familia?

912
00:50:54,886 --> 00:50:56,095
According to the records,

913
00:50:56,179 --> 00:50:57,972
Patricia gave out a statement…

914
00:50:58,055 --> 00:50:59,182
I think…

915
00:50:59,932 --> 00:51:01,476
there's only one person behind this.

916
00:51:01,559 --> 00:51:03,227
Just like how a video
was also created back then

917
00:51:03,311 --> 00:51:05,563
about La Familia's past tragedy.

918
00:51:05,772 --> 00:51:07,190
I did some research.

919
00:51:08,775 --> 00:51:11,360
Patricia's statement back then
barely had any coverage.

920
00:51:12,612 --> 00:51:14,655
You've deleted almost all traces of it.

921
00:51:15,406 --> 00:51:17,366
Because it isn't true.

922
00:51:19,452 --> 00:51:20,661
Which means…

923
00:51:21,078 --> 00:51:23,664
only a few people know of this.

924
00:51:25,166 --> 00:51:26,709
The poisoning…

925
00:51:27,043 --> 00:51:29,879
happened on the same day
as La Familia's anniversary

926
00:51:29,962 --> 00:51:31,214
and the fire.

927
00:51:31,839 --> 00:51:33,508
About the fire incident,

928
00:51:33,591 --> 00:51:36,594
looks like the person behind this
knows a lot about

929
00:51:36,677 --> 00:51:38,471
the inner workings of La Familia.

930
00:51:40,598 --> 00:51:41,974
An inside job?

931
00:51:43,434 --> 00:51:45,770
I want that person to rot in prison.

932
00:51:46,646 --> 00:51:47,772
Diana…

933
00:51:48,189 --> 00:51:51,484
is there something about the fire incident

934
00:51:51,567 --> 00:51:53,820
that could damage
the company's reputation?

935
00:51:54,654 --> 00:51:56,155
Excuse me?

936
00:51:59,700 --> 00:52:01,327
Did you have anything to do with the fire?

937
00:52:01,953 --> 00:52:03,621
How dare you?

938
00:52:04,121 --> 00:52:05,540
What kind of question is that?

939
00:52:05,623 --> 00:52:07,750
My own father died in that incident.

940
00:52:08,417 --> 00:52:09,710
I'm just trying to make sure.

941
00:52:10,461 --> 00:52:11,462
No!

942
00:52:11,921 --> 00:52:13,965
That video spouted nothing but lies!

943
00:52:14,799 --> 00:52:17,885
It was a disgruntled employee
who started the fire.

944
00:52:18,344 --> 00:52:20,346
And it almost led to our collapse.

945
00:52:21,764 --> 00:52:23,933
But whoever is behind this,

946
00:52:25,184 --> 00:52:26,519
they must know something…

947
00:52:28,771 --> 00:52:31,148
that isn't easily known to just anyone.

948
00:52:31,399 --> 00:52:32,900
That's what's scary.

949
00:52:34,402 --> 00:52:35,778
Because they know you.

950
00:52:44,453 --> 00:52:46,163
And whoever they are…

951
00:52:47,874 --> 00:52:49,458
they have a grudge against you.

952
00:52:51,878 --> 00:52:53,462
The huge fire incident from then…

953
00:52:53,963 --> 00:52:55,882
that is still unsolved today.

954
00:52:55,965 --> 00:52:58,843
Mommy! Mommy!

955
00:52:58,926 --> 00:53:00,553
It's possible that Diana Aragon

956
00:53:00,636 --> 00:53:02,138
has something to do with it.

957
00:53:02,555 --> 00:53:04,390
Stop watching that.

958
00:53:04,473 --> 00:53:05,766
But Pa, is it really true?

959
00:53:06,058 --> 00:53:08,311
That the fire was set on purpose
to get the insurance money?

960
00:53:08,394 --> 00:53:09,854
Uh… yes.

961
00:53:09,937 --> 00:53:12,565
It was set on fire by a wacko employee.

962
00:53:13,149 --> 00:53:15,318
They also said that Sis knows something.

963
00:53:15,401 --> 00:53:16,986
-Think it's true?
-Why don't you ask her then?

964
00:53:17,069 --> 00:53:18,112
Hey.

965
00:53:18,529 --> 00:53:19,822
You two,

966
00:53:19,906 --> 00:53:22,491
don't ever ask your sister about this!

967
00:53:22,825 --> 00:53:25,411
-Why not, Pa?
-Just don't.

968
00:53:26,245 --> 00:53:28,331
Let's leave it all in the past.

969
00:53:39,133 --> 00:53:40,593
You called for me?

970
00:53:56,817 --> 00:53:58,110
Patricia.

971
00:53:59,445 --> 00:54:00,821
Tell me the truth.

972
00:54:01,822 --> 00:54:03,115
What truth?

973
00:54:03,658 --> 00:54:07,954
Is this video another one
of your family's schemes?

974
00:54:09,455 --> 00:54:11,707
I don't know anything about it.

975
00:54:13,125 --> 00:54:15,336
This isn't the first time it happened.

976
00:54:18,297 --> 00:54:19,548
First,

977
00:54:19,632 --> 00:54:21,676
it was when I kicked you out of my house.

978
00:54:24,053 --> 00:54:25,388
And now,

979
00:54:27,181 --> 00:54:29,767
it's after your father caused
a scene here.

980
00:54:30,518 --> 00:54:33,729
If we made that video, I won't lie to you.

981
00:54:34,772 --> 00:54:36,232
But would you look at that.

982
00:54:36,857 --> 00:54:38,943
The past has a habit of coming back.

983
00:54:40,027 --> 00:54:41,654
No matter how much you try to bury it.

984
00:54:42,029 --> 00:54:43,531
What do you mean?

985
00:54:43,990 --> 00:54:46,784
When you tried to pin the blame
on me for the fire.

986
00:54:46,867 --> 00:54:48,911
You don't know what you're saying.

987
00:54:51,998 --> 00:54:54,458
Are you going to disregard
my own experiences too?

988
00:54:56,002 --> 00:55:01,257
Just like how you repeatedly made me feel
that what happened was all my fault.

989
00:55:01,340 --> 00:55:03,968
That it was my fault grandfather died.

990
00:55:04,510 --> 00:55:06,929
But now that everything's
rising up to the surface again…

991
00:55:08,389 --> 00:55:09,974
will you tell me the truth?

992
00:55:11,642 --> 00:55:14,311
Was the fire done on purpose
to save the company?

993
00:55:15,021 --> 00:55:18,107
I still remember what you told me
when I was a kid

994
00:55:18,190 --> 00:55:20,192
when the investigators
were interrogating me.

995
00:55:25,322 --> 00:55:27,867
You really believe I'm capable
of doing such a thing?

996
00:55:28,617 --> 00:55:31,203
That I can do such a thing
to my own father?

997
00:55:31,287 --> 00:55:33,706
Is that really how you see me?

998
00:55:34,915 --> 00:55:36,208
All I know…

999
00:55:37,793 --> 00:55:39,503
is that you'll do anything

1000
00:55:39,587 --> 00:55:43,340
and sacrifice everything
just for La Familia.

1001
00:56:20,711 --> 00:56:21,754
Uh, ma'am,

1002
00:56:21,837 --> 00:56:24,632
this is the result
of the investigation of our team.

1003
00:56:24,924 --> 00:56:27,009
We also made sure that…

1004
00:56:27,760 --> 00:56:30,429
all of the evidence pointing to Patricia

1005
00:56:30,846 --> 00:56:31,680
has been erased.

1006
00:56:32,681 --> 00:56:35,309
The result of the investigation
by the fire investigators

1007
00:56:35,392 --> 00:56:38,729
will reflect that as well.

1008
00:56:38,813 --> 00:56:41,690
And by the way,
I've already talked to someone

1009
00:56:41,982 --> 00:56:44,568
so that all of this will be blamed

1010
00:56:44,652 --> 00:56:46,987
on Cecilia Pineda.

1011
00:56:47,905 --> 00:56:49,740
Make sure nothing about this gets out.

1012
00:56:50,449 --> 00:56:51,700
Yes, ma'am.

1013
00:56:52,326 --> 00:56:55,329
I've already made sure
that everyone's lips are sealed.

1014
00:56:59,416 --> 00:57:00,918
I'm sorry, Papa.

1015
00:57:01,919 --> 00:57:03,879
I've done everything.

1016
00:57:04,922 --> 00:57:06,966
For the sake of everything.

1017
00:57:07,508 --> 00:57:08,926
Of the company…

1018
00:57:10,219 --> 00:57:11,470
and most of all,

1019
00:57:12,888 --> 00:57:15,891
I have to protect Patricia.

1020
00:58:19,330 --> 00:58:21,332
What's important is that
you and Patricia are seen together.

1021
00:58:21,415 --> 00:58:23,626
You need to show them a united front.

1022
00:58:23,709 --> 00:58:25,127
Seems like you don't want me here anyway.

1023
00:58:25,211 --> 00:58:27,588
Who told you that I don't want you here?

1024
00:58:27,671 --> 00:58:29,798
I can finally do what I've always wanted.

1025
00:58:29,882 --> 00:58:31,300
I like it because I worked for it.

1026
00:58:31,675 --> 00:58:34,011
I gave it my all,
not just because I'm an Aragon.

1027
00:58:34,094 --> 00:58:35,346
Do you think they're planning something?

1028
00:58:35,429 --> 00:58:37,181
All I know is
I can't be kicked out of here.

1029
00:58:37,264 --> 00:58:39,016
There is someone
who wants to take the company down.

1030
00:58:39,099 --> 00:58:43,103
I will never allow anybody
to take down La Familia.

1031
00:58:44,104 --> 00:58:45,981
-What was that?
-Help!
